---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { beacon } from '../lib/analytics';
import { formatPhone } from '../lib/seo';
import { site } from '../lib/site';

const { address } = site;

const contents = [
  { id: 'what-we-collect', label: 'What we collect' },
  { id: 'how-we-use-it', label: 'How we use it' },
  { id: 'cookies-and-analytics', label: 'Cookies and analytics' },
  { id: 'spam-protection', label: 'Spam protection' },
  { id: 'technical-records', label: 'Technical records' },
  { id: 'questions', label: 'Questions' },
  { id: 'changes', label: 'Changes to this page' },
];
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description={`What ${site.name} collects when you visit this website or send us a message, and what we do with it.`}
  intro="We collect very little. This page explains what, why, and who to ask if you have a question."
  updated="2026-11-23"
  contents={contents}
>
  <h2 id="what-we-collect">What we collect</h2>
  <p>
    The only personal information this website collects is what you type into our project inquiry
    form:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>your name</li>
    <li>your email address</li>
    <li>your phone number, if you choose to give it</li>
    <li>the type of project you have in mind</li>
    <li>your message</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not ask you to create an account, and we do not collect anything else about you.</p>

  <h2 id="how-we-use-it">How we use it</h2>
  <p>
    When you send the form, it is emailed to our office so that we can reply to you about your
    project. This website does not keep a copy: it has no database and no list of past messages. The
    email in our inbox is our record.
  </p>
  <p>
    The email is delivered by Resend, an email delivery service, which keeps a copy of sent messages
    for a limited time (currently 30 days) so that it can deliver them and show whether they
    arrived. Resend describes how it handles that information in its own privacy policy.
  </p>
  <p>We do not sell your information or share it for advertising.</p>

  <h2 id="cookies-and-analytics">Cookies and analytics</h2>
  <p>
    This website sets no cookies. Its fonts are served from the site itself, so your browser does
    not contact font services either.
  </p>
  {/* Matches what the site does: the analytics paragraph appears only when the beacon is on. */}
  {beacon ? (
    <p>
      We count visits with Cloudflare Web Analytics, which tells us how many people visit, which
      pages they read and how quickly the pages load. It sets no cookies, stores nothing in your
      browser and does not follow you from site to site. For each page view it records the page
      address (without anything after a question mark), the page you came from, your browser and
      type of device, your country, and loading times. Cloudflare says it does not use this to
      identify or fingerprint visitors, and describes its handling in its own privacy policy.
    </p>
  ) : (
    <p>
      This website does not collect visitor statistics. If we add them later, we will use a
      cookieless tool that does not follow you from site to site, and we will update this page
      first.
    </p>
  )}

  <h2 id="spam-protection">Spam protection</h2>
  <p>
    The inquiry form uses Cloudflare Turnstile, a spam check, to tell people from automated
    programs. It runs only on the form, and Cloudflare may look at technical details of your browser
    and connection to do its job. Cloudflare describes how it handles that information in its own
    privacy policy.
  </p>

  <h2 id="technical-records">Technical records</h2>
  <p>
    Like most websites, this one is delivered by a hosting provider, Cloudflare. In the ordinary
    course of delivering pages, a hosting provider can see technical details of each request, such
    as the address it came from. We do not use that information to identify visitors.
  </p>

  <h2 id="questions">Questions</h2>
  <p>
    If you have a question about this page, or about a message you sent us, get in touch through our{' '}
    <a href="/contact/">contact page</a> or write to us:
  </p>
  <address>
    <p>{site.legalName}</p>
    <p>{address.street}</p>
    <p>
      {address.city}, {address.region} {address.postalCode}
    </p>
    {site.phone && <p>{formatPhone(site.phone)}</p>}
  </address>

  <h2 id="changes">Changes to this page</h2>
  <p>
    If what we collect or how we use it changes, we will update this page and the date at the top.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
